KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp23
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ builtin param type: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
A function parameter declared with a type-yielding builtin AND a name,
`int probe(__add_rvalue_reference(_Tp) v)`, is a PARSE error ("parse
error before ') { return v'") -- the builtin-call form followed by a
declarator name confuses the cast-vs-declaration disambiguation.  The
unnamed form parses.  gcc-16 headers use the named form
(is_trivially_move_assignable_v's helper).  VALIDITY: gcc-16-only
builtin; certified by g++ 16.2 in the gcc16-gate docker image
(tumbleweed); host g++ 13 does not know the builtin.
Derived from the cvise-reduced gcc16_optional_transform artifact
(round 106 manual backward delta, /tmp/k106 h1-h4).
